865 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Amdahl\031s Law assumes a fixed problem size \050Strong Scaling\051\054 meaning the serial fraction \0501 \055 p\051 acts as an immutable bottleneck\056 As core counts increase toward infinity\054 the execution time becomes entirely dominated by the non\055parallelizable code segment\054 causing theoretical speedup to hard\055saturate at 1\057\0501\055p\051\056 Conversely\054 Gustafson\031s Law evaluates Weak Scaling\054 where the problem size scales proportionally alongside core count\056 Under Gustafson\047s model\054 the workload assigned to parallel cores grows while the serial execution overhead remains constant in time\054 rendering the sequential bottleneck negligible and predicting near\055linear speedup approx on a 64\055core system\056)
     /K [ 29 ]
     /P 866 0 R
     /Pg 804 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

